WEBVTT

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.690
It's starting to smell like summer, isn't it?

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:15.740
Yeah.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.820
It's easy to tell the seasons
apart in Japan, isn't it?

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.280
Yes. Summer is hot, winter is cold,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.250
and spring and fall are comfortable.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:29.000
The weather changes all the time in England.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.430
They say you can experience
lots of seasons in a single day.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.130
Yeah, I remember.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.510
Out of nowhere, rain will start falling...

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.010
Or garbage.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.600
Shino!

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.820
Or Karens!

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.960
This happens all the time in England.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:47.730
No, it doesn't!

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.060
Karen, what are you doing?!

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.810
I'm getting heat stroke.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.740
It's not even that hot yet!

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.420
No! Summer's just around the corner!

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.990
You mustn't let the seasons pass you by!

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.500
Kujou Karen: summer model!

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:07.000
<i>It's... It's so ugly...</i>

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.780
Karen, you look like a rocker on
her way home from a band trip.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.000
A what?!

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:15.470
Oh, yeah. My outfit's theme is "wild."

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.100
Did you buy that?

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.590
No, I made it myself.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.000
You made it yourself?!

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:25.810
It's still a little chilly at night.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.120
Morning!

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.700
Good morning.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:29.790
Morning.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:30.830
Morning!

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:32.610
Good mornin'!

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.190
What's with the sleeveless look?

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:38.890
Karen, Kuzehashi-sensei will scold you again

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.120
if you don't wear your blouse.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:42.870
It's fine.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:45.840
This look is super cool.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.890
She might even call your parents this time.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.400
Rustle

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.130
What? She actually listened!

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.130
Is this okay?

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.430
Your parents...

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.600
Youko, your hair is a mess.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.290
Let me hold your bag.

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:08.390
Do you want some snacks?

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.450
I'll carry you to school!

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:14.630
Don't overdo it.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.280
Do Not Enter

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:24.340
Don't worry. I won't tell.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.910
Karen's mum is scary when she's mad.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:31.290
Actually, the other day...

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:36.880
Karen! I've heard a rumor that you've been
causing trouble for your homeroom teacher.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.300
That's not good.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:45.810
As a penalty, I will eat a piece of
super yummy cake in front of you.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.690
Please! Have mercy on me!

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:50.690
No way.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:52.930
So scary...

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.670
Hey, we're leaving you behind.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.020
It's almost summer vacation, huh?

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.200
That's almost two months away.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.200
Huh? Is it?

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.100
Um...

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:10.960
What's wrong?

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.730
My mom always tells me I should be sweeter.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.460
Please tell me if I'm being too loud.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.210
What?

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:22.870
You can't mean that!
Your energy is your best feature!

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:23.840
But...

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.730
You and Alice are my angels!

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.980
Every day, I feel like
I'm ascending to heaven!

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.920
Don't you agree, Aya-chan?

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:34.010
<i>Why is she asking me?!</i>

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:36.480
Y-Yeah... You're angels!

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:16.580
Episode 7
My Dear Hero

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:13.580
Good morning.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.060
Good morning.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.870
Good morning.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.680
Everyone's changed into
their summer uniforms.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.530
It <i>is</i> hot today.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.100
Good morning.

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:24.540
Good morning.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.460
Good morning.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.140
Don't you wear lighter clothes in the summer?

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.650
Th-These <i>are</i> my summer clothes...

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:35.040
Do they seem too stuffy?

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.150
No, I just thought you might
like to change your look.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:41.080
I think something cute
would be nice for summer.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:43.370
Cute? But...

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.370
For example...

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.640
How about this?

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.360
A-An animal costume?

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.710
I found it in a locker.

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:54.360
<i>What happened to lighter summer wear?</i>

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.270
I'll see if I can handle
wearing it in the summer.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:58.920
What? Maybe you shouldn't...

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.560
Good morning.

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:03.460
Good morning.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.930
Good morning.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.010
G-Good morning...

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.030
I couldn't do it.

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:17.430
Sensei! You did this for me?!

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:28.950
See you later!

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:30.450
Bye.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:31.490
See you tomorrow.

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:37.000
Sorry! I'm leaving early today!

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:38.780
You have something to do?

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:41.750
My dad bought me a
limited edition necklace

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.640
that I've been wanting!

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:45.130
That's great, Karen.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.050
See you tomorrow!

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.990
What's going on with Karen?

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:55.790
Her dad bought her a necklace.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:57.700
She seemed in a good mood.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:01.200
Karen and her dad are really close.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.440
Her papa's kid, huh?

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.610
"Papakid" sounds kinda cool!

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.020
Like something tasty!

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:07.440
Growl

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:10.950
Coming.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:12.910
Maybe it's a delivery?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.580
Who is it?

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:16.700
Huh?

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:17.760
Karen?!

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:20.530
What's wrong? I thought you went home!

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:22.080
Did something happen?

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:26.250
Oh, there you are! I've been looking for you!
I came all the way here as I am so shocked,

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.170
but don't worry, I already called
Mom. Please listen to me!

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.800
It's my dad. He was lying to me.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.760
I really wanted to know the truth,
even though he said it was for my sake.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.600
But he made me feel like an idiot
for being pleased with his words.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.540
I dislike... <i>hate</i> my dad!
I'm not going to go home anymore!

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:39.540
Too fast!

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.380
What did she say?

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:44.420
She had a fight with her dad
and ran away from home.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:45.230
She ran away?!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:49.140
My dad said he couldn't buy the necklace.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:51.090
He lied about getting it,

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:53.740
because he didn't want to make me sad.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:57.860
Kind lies can hurt people sometimes.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:58.620
Alice?

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:02.160
But it's not your dad's fault.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.190
You can still make up with—

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:07.840
No! I'm staying here tonight!

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:08.590
What?!

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:12.620
Please! I already called my mom...

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:15.640
I can't face my dad.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:19.140
Y-You can't. You'll inconvenience Shino's family.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:22.130
I'd actually be happy to have you stay over!

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:23.020
Shino?!

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:26.030
Please! I won't bother anyone!

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:29.170
Two blonde girls?

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:32.500
Sure. Stay as long as you like.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:33.650
Even your mom?!

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:36.120
I'm home.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:42.480
Welcome home. You must
be tired after your shoot.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.150
I'll take your bag.

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:46.680
Huh? It's Karen-chan.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:48.840
That's a great angle!

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:53.700
You're beautiful from every angle, Isami!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.720
What's going on?

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:57.340
I see...

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.840
Karen-chan ran away from home, huh?

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:02.890
Ta-da!

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:06.640
Her uniform would get wrinkled
if she wore it all the time,

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.480
so I gave her some of my clothes.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:11.980
<i>That's the dress that didn't
look good on Shinobu.</i>

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.590
I feel like I'm on a home stay.

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:16.970
I always wanted to try one.

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:18.580
It does, doesn't it?

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:20.160
It does!

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:23.940
This is enough space for me.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:25.480
You're going to live here?!

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.930
Let's dig in!

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.430
Japanese food! It looks delicious!

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:34.150
Shino's mum makes great Japanese food.

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:37.040
My mom is English,

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:38.590
so we have mostly Western meals.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:41.130
Really? What's her specialty?

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:42.770
Meat pies!

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:46.950
It's delicious.

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:50.270
This miso soup tastes just
like Mom's home cooking.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:52.150
Not meat pies?

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.400
Thank you for dinner.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:57.630
That was delicious.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.580
You're welcome.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.700
I'll help you clean up!

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:06.350
Oh, that's all right. You can stay seated.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.190
Please let me help!

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:11.890
Really? Thank you.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:13.150
Excuse me!

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:19.660
Alice?

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:21.650
Thanks for dinner!

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:23.780
A-Are you okay?

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.570
I'll help, too!

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:29.060
Huh?

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:31.240
Alice, you're crowding me!

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:34.300
It's not fair for you to score points by yourself!

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:33.700
Oh, dear...

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:36.860
Where did they pick that up?

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:39.790
<i>I think I can do it today.</i>

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:44.130
<i>If we take separate baths, it'll take too long,
so I'll suggest we get in together...</i>

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:49.510
Karen, you're using too much shampoo!

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:51.860
What? This is a normal amount!

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:52.750
Huh?

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:01.300
They left me out...

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:05.760
You can't fit three people in that tiny tub.

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:12.760
I had fun in Shino's bath, too!

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.330
Karen.

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.880
It's okay if you stay here,

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:20.030
but you should still talk to your dad.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:25.530
Okay. I'll call him later.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:27.820
Okay.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:39.210
<i>I hope Karen and her dad make up...</i>

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:45.930
Dad? I'm sorry for getting angry,
but I've calmed down now.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:50.930
Really? Thank you so much! I love you, Dad!

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:54.380
Alice, listen to this!

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:57.160
My dad used his influence to get the necklace!

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:59.780
My dad is so awesome!

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.570
R-Really?

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:05.570
I know. I'm going to share
my happiness with everyone.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:09.430
Karen?

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:12.080
What's going on? You don't often call me.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:16.490
I'm going to give you some of my happiness!

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.590
Oh? Karen?

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:23.840
I'm going to give you some happiness!

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.490
Some what?

00:12:26.150 --> 00:12:28.470
You're always so full of energy.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:29.980
Of course!

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:33.980
Any day, anytime, anywhere!
I'm always full of energy!

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:37.650
I'm glad you made up with your dad.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.780
It's thanks to Alice's advice!

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.230
Alice is my hero!

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:44.490
I'm your older sister!

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:49.230
Well, ready to go to bed?

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:50.900
What? It's so early.

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.140
It's not even ten yet.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:56.670
Karen, would you like to sleep in my bed?

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.030
You can't do that!

00:12:58.030 --> 00:13:00.750
It's not big enough for two, and Karen
moves around a lot in her sleep!

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:02.500
It's okay.

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:04.340
We can put Karen on the wall side,

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:05.050
Kick!

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:07.660
so even if I fall out of bed,
I'll still be in heaven.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:09.010
Thud

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.010
More like hell!

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:13.180
I enjoyed our spontaneous sleepover today.

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:15.410
Thank you for letting me stay.

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:17.210
Next time, you can do a home stay

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:19.520
at my house in England.

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:22.780
Shino, you've seen Karen's house.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:25.640
It's huge, like a castle.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:28.030
Oh, yeah, I did see it once...

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:31.040
You can all come at the same time!

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:33.780
We can even handle a hundred guests at a time!

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:35.040
Yeah!

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:39.850
Somehow, it doesn't sound like
it would be that big anymore.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:42.110
We should go to sleep now.

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:43.920
I'm turning off the light.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.700
Goodnight, Alice and Karen.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.370
Goodnight!

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.110
Goodnight, Shino and Karen.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.130
Jeez, Karen...

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.940
You took all my covers.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:08.060
Wake up, you two. We're going to be late.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.870
Hurry up.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.310
Five more minutes...

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:15.980
Ten more minutes, Mum...

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:18.460
You're hopeless.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.620
Fine. Ten more seconds.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.520
One...

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:24.900
Come on!

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:27.220
There are three of you!
You shouldn't <i>all</i> be sleeping!

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:31.580
Karen called me last night.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:33.870
You, too? She called me, too.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:36.590
It didn't seem like she really needed anything.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.680
Good morning.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:40.750
Good morning.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:42.110
Mornin'.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.140
Good morning.

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:44.680
Huh? Karen?

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:47.560
Why did you show up with Shino and Alice?

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:49.850
Isn't your house the other way?

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:53.870
Well, actually, yesterday...

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:57.870
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:01.920
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:09.180
When we were little,
Alice always played the hero.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.480
What? That's surprising.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:15.210
Wait, you didn't play house?

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:16.930
You played monsters?

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:22.150
I can only picture Karen dragging
Alice around, both then and now.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:24.640
Yeah, she seems like my younger sister now.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:25.070
What?

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:29.220
But I've always respected you, Alice.

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:31.070
Really?

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:35.260
I only know Alice from now
and during my home stay.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:38.330
I'd like to hear more stories
from when you were younger.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.700
Me, too.

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:40.660
Same here!

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:43.670
You got it!

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:47.470
Okay... This happened after you went back

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:49.670
to Japan after your home stay.

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:57.020
Hi!

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:57.680
Hi.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:02.190
Hi, Alice! Let's go out and play!

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:07.340
I-ro-ha-ni-ho-he-to...

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:12.700
Scribble

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.650
Chi-ri-nu-ru-wo...

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:12.700
Alice was writing Japanese characters
like she was possessed by something.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:12.720
Wa-ka-yo-ta-re-so...

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:15.350
I was just concentrating!

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:18.910
Scribble

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:18.910
Ki-yu-me-mi-shi we-hi-mo-se-su...

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:21.210
Alice, are you studying Japanese again?
We don't have lessons with my dad today.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:24.710
Preparation and review are important, though.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.840
Hmm... I don't know.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.960
Come on! Let's go out!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:39.220
Scribble
Scribble

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.720
Not now. I am a little—

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:37.350
It's boring! I am bored! Let's play!
I've got nothing to do!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.220
Sorry. Later.

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:41.980
Scribble

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.980
Guess what? My dad has a fun
Japanese game! I will get it!

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.370
Huh?

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:08.040
Huh? Karen? She stormed out a while ago.
She hasn't been here since then.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.800
Wait! Where are you off to?

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:15.550
Just around!

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:39.830
That's... Karen's shoe!

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:54.420
Karen! Can you hear me? Karen!

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.850
Huh?

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:05.730
Did I just hear something?

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:10.730
How come I'm sleeping here? Let's see...

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.490
Kitty!

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:32.920
Oh, yeah. I slipped and fell, and...

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:37.970
I was so careless. Oh, dear.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.890
Ouch!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:44.770
Did I sprain my ankle? I'm stuck!

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:52.400
Oh...

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.020
Alice!

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:56.940
<i>Alice never listens to me.</i>

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:59.740
<i>She's always looking at the kokeshi doll.</i>

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.950
<i>She doesn't care about me...</i>

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:07.040
Karen! Can you hear me?

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:10.290
Karen! Karen!

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.670
Alice!

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:16.320
Karen!

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.300
Karen! Where are you?

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:25.180
<i>Alice is almost gone!</i>

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:28.180
Alice! I'm here!

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:32.230
Alice!

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:40.950
What should I do? What should I do?

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:47.540
"Tsu" and "ka." That's the
Japanese all-purpose password.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:49.780
Tsu!

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:51.960
Tsu!

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.070
Karen!

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.460
Tsu!

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:54.710
Tsu!

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.290
Tsu!

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:58.210
Karen! Are you okay?

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:00.280
Alice...

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:04.710
Tsu! Tsu!

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:07.200
Tsu! Tsu, tsu!

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.600
What's "tsu"?

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:08.600
Tsu!

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:13.150
I almost died...

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:14.860
Don't exaggerate.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:19.690
Alice, thank you for searching for me.

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:22.950
Why not?

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.990
That's what friends are for.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:30.700
Then, Alice left for Japan

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.720
without even telling me!

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:36.720
That's because you were on a trip!

00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:39.250
Alice can be surprisingly reckless.

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:41.040
<i>But...</i>

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:45.960
<i>I'm not one to talk.</i>

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:53.310
Karen, is your foot okay?

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:54.190
Huh?

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:56.490
She sprained it in PE.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:59.190
It doesn't hurt anymore. I'm fine.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:03.950
See you tomorrow, everyone!

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:05.010
Okay.

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:05.840
See you later.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:06.810
Be careful.

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:07.630
Wait!

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:09.200
Huh?

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.000
I'll walk you home.

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:12.990
I'll go with you...

00:21:12.990 --> 00:21:14.420
Now, now.

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:16.130
Let them be together sometimes.

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:22.650
You're still my hero, Alice.

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:24.970
I told you, I'm your older sister!

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:26.470
Then what's Shino?

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:29.460
Shino's <i>our</i> hero.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:31.550
Yes!

00:23:06.510 --> 00:23:07.950
I'm home.

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:08.780
Yes!

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:12.850
It's been 30 minutes, and she's still not home!

00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:14.950
Yes!

00:23:15.230 --> 00:23:19.210
She's a blonde high schooler who
looks like a grade school student!

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:20.460
Shino...

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:24.290
I want to be the hero, too!

00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:27.040
Okay, then. This time, I will be the monster.

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:28.810
Karen Boomerang!

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:29.170
Crash

00:23:28.810 --> 00:23:29.560
Oops!

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:31.180
Dash

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:31.720
The monster is coming!

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:36.060
#8 Almost Summer Vacation

00:23:32.130 --> 00:23:34.360
We're sorry!
